course: dictionary
lesson: 3643
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. Fireball is a noun with three meanings: a ball of fire, a very bright meteor, and (informally) a lively, energetic person.
explain: «A fireball is a meteor brighter than the planet Venus» is about space. «Never put water on hot oil: it explodes into a fireball of burning fat» is about danger in the kitchen. The words around fireball are the clues.
explain: Check by swapping in your meaning. A very bright shooting star fits the sky. A ball of fire from an explosion fits the kitchen. If your meaning makes no sense in the sentence, try the next meaning.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A fireball is a ball of fire, such as one made by an explosion.
fact: A fireball is also a very bright meteor, a shooting star that burns up in the sky.
fact: In informal speech, a fireball is a lively, energetic person.
fact: «Fireball» can be a noun for a ball of fire, a meteor, or a person, so always check the context.
exercise: «It bursts up and flings burning oil into the air as a fireball.» What is the fireball here? | *A ball of fire from an explosion | A cold, wet puddle | A lively, energetic person | A bright shooting star
exercise: «A fireball is a meteor brighter than the planet Venus.» In this sentence, what is a fireball? | A ball of wet snow | *A very bright meteor, a shooting star that burns up | A kind of kitchen pan | A lively, energetic person
exercise: Mia says, «You're such a fireball at parties!» What does she mean? | *A lively, energetic person | A ball of fire from an explosion | A tired, sleepy child | A very bright meteor
test: Why must you never throw water on burning oil? | It puts the fire out at once every time | *It turns to steam and throws the oil out in a fireball | It makes the oil cold | It makes the pan clean
test: In «a fireball in the sky», what does fireball most likely mean? | A mirror in the sky | A bird with red feathers | *A very bright meteor burning up | A kite flying high
exam: What is the safe first step with a burning oil pan? | Run outside carrying the pan | Pour the oil down the sink | *Turn off the heat if it is safe, and call a grown-up | Throw water on it to cool it down
